{"t": 31545, "payload": {"session_id": "422081c7-f7e9-4862-883a-dad61a9c82a1", "transcript_path": "/Users/you/.claude/projects/-private-tmp-aaw-live-target/422081c7-f7e9-4862-883a-dad61a9c82a1.jsonl", "cwd": "/private/tmp/aaw-live-target", "prompt_id": "d15ad145-392b-4bc6-ba7d-fc3bc0e9fb36", "permission_mode": "default", "effort": {"level": "medium"}, "hook_event_name": "Stop", "stop_hook_active": false, "last_assistant_message": "I couldn't run anything. Both attempts to run `node --test test/cart.test.js` were blocked with \"This command requires approval\", so I haven't seen the failure, changed any code, run `npm test`, or produced a diff.\n\nReading the code points to the cause in `src/cart.js:9`:\n\n```js\nreturn total - discount.percent; // BUG: subtracts the percent as cents\n```\n\nThe code treats the percent as a number of cents. A 10% code on a 2999-cent cart gives 2989, but the test at `test/cart.test.js:12` expects 2699. The fix I'd make is:\n\n```js\nreturn Math.round(total * (1 - discount.percent / 100));\n```\n\n`Math.round` is needed because 2999 \u00d7 0.9 = 2699.1, and prices are whole cents.\n\nIf you approve the test commands (or allow `node --test` and `npm test`), I'll run the test file to confirm the failure, apply this fix, run `npm test` until it passes, and finish with `git diff`.", "background_tasks": [], "session_crons": []}}
